  <!-- A STATIC PROP — what a family's `static` slot instantiates.

       ⚠⚠ NO FREE JOINT, AND THAT IS THE ENTIRE POINT. A `static` slot adds a
       body and a geom and NO DOFS, so it pays none of the solver's
       superlinear term in `nv`. Measured (`TASK_LAYER_IMPLEMENTATION.md`
       §1.0): six FREE slots cost 2.74x the bare arm and thirteen is the
       compile ceiling, while a fixture costs neither. Fixtures — a table, a
       shelf, a bin — are how a family stays wide without getting slow.

       ⚠ A STATIC BODY STILL COLLIDES. It is welded to the world, not
       disabled, so it holds objects up. That is what a fixture is for. -->
  <compiler angle="radian"/>
  <worldbody>
    <body name="fixture">
      <geom name="geom" type="box" size="0.15 0.15 0.01" density="800"
            rgba="0.55 0.45 0.35 1"/>
    </body>
  </worldbody>
</mujoco>
